---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_273",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 273,
  "text": "[[1059.11]] <b>225.  Marginalien zu Jungius' Logica Hamburgensis [Herbst 1678 bis Winter 1679/80 (?)]</b>\n [[1059.12]] <tab/>[Herbst 1678 bis Winter 1679/80 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[1059.19]] <k>logicae generalis</k> <k>Liber Primus.</k> <i>De Notionibus.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1059.20]] <k>Cap. V.</k> De Praedicamento Quantitatis. </p>\n<p> [[1059.21]] 17. <i>Curva non plana</i> est, quae in plano sita esse nequit, <Fn><i>Am Rande</i>: ^&.!! <Leibniz special character: distilletur></Fn> uti sunt, <i>Helix cylindracea</i>,\n[[1059.22]] <i>Helix conica</i>, <i>Helix sphaerica</i>, quarum quaelibet <b>non nisi</b> <Fn>Imo si moveatur, dabit superficiem in qua locatur.</Fn> in ea, unde denominatur,\n[[1059.23]] superficie locari potest. </p>\n<p> [[1060.1]] <k>Logicae Generalis liber ii.</k> De Enuntiatione. </p>\n<p> [[1060.2]] <k>Cap. XIII.</k> De Enuntiatione Conjuncta, et in specie de Connexa. </p>\n<p> [[1060.3]] 14. Non requiritur ad veritatem Connexae, ut membrum ejus aliquod categorice\n[[1060.4]] verum sit, sed hoc tantum, ut <i>in affirmata</i> Antecedente posito, etiam consequens ponendum\n[[1060.5]] sit, ut <i>Si asinus volat, asinus est alatus</i>, hic utrumque membrum categorice falsum\n[[1060.6]] est, Tota tamen Enuntiatio est verissima. </p>\n<p> [[1060.7]] 15. In <i>negata</i> vero hoc requiritur, ut Consequens ex Antecedente non sequatur, ut\n[[1060.8]] <i>Non, <b>si asinus volat, pennas</i> <i>habet</i>. <Fn>Licet <tab/>aliud: <i>Si asinus volat pennas non habet</i>  <tab/>Negans ut <i>non omnis</i>, et <i>omnis non</i></Fn> Ita Cic. pro Rosc. Amer. <i>Non continuo, si me\n[[1060.9]] in sicariorum gregem contuli, sicarius sum.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1060.10]] <k>Cap. XVI.</k> De Disjuncta Enuntiatione. </p>\n<p> [[1060.11]] 7. <i>Incomplete disjunctiva</i> Enuntiatio a Jurisconsultis <i>Subdisjunctiva</i> appellatur et\n[[1060.12]] duplex est, prior <i>tantum ponens</i>, posterior <i>tantum tollens.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1060.13]] 8. <i>Prior</i> est, quae alterum duorum, vel etiam unum e pluribus necessario esse\n[[1060.14]] significat, ita tamen ut permittat, utrumque vel omnia simul esse. </p>\n<p> [[1060.15]] 9. Et haec Connexis aequipollet illis tantum, quae uno membro negato reliquum, vel\n[[1060.16]] reliqua affirmant. Ut si Medicus dicat aegroto, <i>Aut bibes hunc haustum, aut morieris</i>;\n[[1060.17]] aequipollet ejus assertio hisce duabus Connexis, <i>Si non bibes, morieris; Si non morieris,\n[[1060.18]] bibes.</i> Reliquis duabus non aequipollet, <Fn>Imo haec ex illis sequuntu[r.]</Fn> nimirum hisce, <i>Si bibes, non morieris; Si morieris,\n[[1060.19]] non bibes.</i> Scit enim Medicus, posse eum et bibere, et tamen mori. Talis quoque\n[[1060.20]] disjunctio est, cum Graecus convivij dominus convivae dicit, <greek>^%)­h píui, ^%)­h ^%)/apiui</greek> <i>Aut</i> <i>bibe,\n[[1060.21]] aut abi.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1060.22]] <k>Logicae Generalis liber iii.</k> De Dianoea sive Ratiocinatione. </p>\n<p> [[1060.23]] <k>Cap. XXXI.</k> De Dianoea mixtim composita, et in specie de Syllogismis Quartae\n[[1060.24]] figurae adscriptis. </p>\n<p> [[1060.25]] 2. Mixtim compositarum nonnullae <i>speciem syllogismi Categorici</i> simulant, uti sunt\n[[1060.26]] inprimis <i>syllogismi quartae figurae</i> dicti. </p>\n<p> [[1060.27]] 3. Est autem <i>Quarta Figura</i> dispositio quaedam trium categoricarum enuntiationum\n[[1060.28]] syllogisticae similis, in qua medius terminus est praedicatum in Majore, et subjectum in\n[[1061.1]] Minore sumptione ita, ut sumptione utraque vera existente, vera etiam existat Conclusio,\n[[1061.2]] qualis dispositio est in iis, quae sequuntur:\n [[1061.3]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character>Item, <tab/><i>E.</i> <tab/><i>Quoddam corpus non est lapis.</i>^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character> <tab/><i>Omnis ars est habitus,\n [[1061.4]] <tab/>Omnis habitus est qualitas</i>, <Fn><i>Ergo omnis ars est qualitas,</i> Unde per conversionem fit <i>Quaedam qualitas est ars</i>.</Fn>\n [[1061.5]] <tab/><i>E. Quaedam qualitas est ars</i>:\n [[1061.6]] Item, <tab/><i>Nullus lapis est arbor</i>, <Fn><i>Nulla arbor est lapis</i></Fn>\n [[1061.7]] <tab/><i>Omnis arbor est corpus</i>,\n [[1061.8]] <tab/><i>E. Quoddam corpus non est lapis.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1061.9]] 4. Est autem syllogismo quidem similis haec ratiocinatio, non tamen syllogismus,\n[[1061.10]] quia <i>Conclusio ex praemissis <b>necessario non</i> <Fn>qui[d]ni</Fn> <i>consequitur</i>, quod praemissae ob\n[[1061.11]] ineptam et <i>minus naturalem terminorum dispositionem</i> intellectum excitare nequeant ad\n[[1061.12]] eliciendam Conclusionem, nisi <i>intermedia</i> alia <i>propositio</i> vel una vel altera interveniat: ut\n[[1061.13]] si in posteriore exemplo propositionem secundo loco interjiciam ita,\n [[1061.14]] <tab/><i>Nullus lapis est arbor</i>,\n [[1061.15]] Fe <tab/><i>E. Nulla arbor est lapis</i>,\n [[1061.16]] lap <tab/><i>Omnis autem arbor est corpus</i>,\n [[1061.17]] ton <tab/><i>E. Quoddam corpus non est lapis.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1061.18]] 5. Jam ex prima propositione necessario consequitur secunda per <i>simplicem Conversionem</i>:\n[[1061.19]] Ex secunda porro et tertia infertur quarta per <i>syllogismum tertiae figurae</i>. Est\n[[1061.20]] itaque ratiocinatio tota ex Consequentia immediata et Syllogismo composita. </p>\n<p> [[1061.21]] 6. Quanquam autem terminus, qui quasi medius est, ipso <i>situ</i> est <i>medius</i>; tamen\n[[1061.22]] <i>extremi termini</i> in Conclusione situm prorsus contrarium <i>adipiscuntur</i> ei, quem in praemissis\n[[1061.23]] obtinebant. </p>\n<p> [[1061.24]] 7. Atque hinc fit, ut aversetur quasi intellectus hanc terminorum dispositionem,\n[[1061.25]] ideoque <i>spuria</i> quasi <i>quaedam figura</i> sit, quae <i>Quarta</i> nuncupatur, ac proinde a consueto\n[[1061.26]] ratiocinandi usu omnino exsulet. </p>\n<p> [[1062.1]] 8. Caeterum quo commodius a genuinis <i>apparentes hi quartae figurae syllogismi</i>\n[[1062.2]] distinguantur, sumptionum metathesi facta, <i>secundum primae figurae ordinem dispositi</i>\n[[1062.3]] in certos Modos, quos <i>indirectos primae figurae Modos</i> vocant, redigi solent, praefixis\n[[1062.4]] <i>trisyllabis voculis</i>, quarum <i>vocales</i> quantitatem et qualitatem, <i>Consonae</i> vero reductionem\n[[1062.5]] ad primae genuinos et directos Modos innuant, non secus atque in imperfectis\n[[1062.6]] Figuris. </p>\n<p> [[1062.7]] 9. Voculae istae technicae quinque sunt, et hoc comprehenduntur rhythmo,\n [[1062.8]] <i>Celantes, Baralip, Dabitis, Fapesmo, Frisesmo.</i>\n[[1062.9]] <petit> </p>\n<p> [[1062.10]] <i>Die folgende Tabelle ist aus Raumgründen in Kleindruck gesetzt</i>:\n [[1062.11]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character><tab/>Fris <tab/><i>E.</i> <tab/><i>Q. aegrum non est animal.</i> <tab/><i>E.</i> <tab/><i>Q. aegrum non est animal.</i> <tab/>rent^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character>\n [[1062.12]] <tab/>I. <tab/>Reductio\n [[1062.13]] <tab/>Ba <tab/><i>O. habitus est qualitas, <tab/>O. habitus est qualitas</i><tab/>Bar\n [[1062.14]] <tab/>ra <tab/><i>O. ars est habitus, <tab/>O. ars est habitus</i>, <tab/>ba\n [[1062.15]] <tab/>lip <tab/><i>E. Q. qualitas est ars. <tab/>E. O. ars est qualitas</i>,<tab/>ra\n [[1062.16]] <tab/><i>E. Q. qualitas est ars.</i>\n [[1062.17]] <tab/>II.\n [[1062.18]] <tab/>Ce <tab/><i>N. arbor sentit, <tab/>N. arbor sentit</i>, <tab/>Ce\n [[1062.19]] <tab/>lan <tab/><i>O. quercus est arbor, <tab/>O. quercus est arbor</i>, <tab/>la\n [[1062.20]] <tab/>tes <tab/><i>E. N. sentiens est quercus. <tab/>E. N. quercus sentit</i>, <tab/>rent\n [[1062.21]] <tab/><i>E. N. sentiens est quercus.</i>\n [[1062.22]] <tab/>III.\n [[1062.23]] <tab/>Da <tab/><i>O. bonum est amandum, <tab/>O. bonum est amandum</i> <tab/>Da\n [[1062.24]] <tab/>bi <tab/><i>Q. labor est bonus, <tab/>Q. labor est bonus</i> <tab/>ri\n [[1062.25]] <tab/>tis <tab/><i>E. Q. amandum est labor. <tab/>E. Q. labor est amandus</i> <tab/>i\n [[1062.26]] <tab/><i>E. Q. amandum est labor.</i>\n [[1062.27]] <tab/>IV.\n [[1062.28]] <tab/>Fap <tab/><i>O. arbor est corpus</i>, <tab/><i>N. arbor est lapis</i>, <tab/>Fe\n [[1062.29]] <tab/>esm <tab/><i>N. lapis est arbor, <tab/>Q. corpus est arbor</i>, <tab/>ri\n [[1062.30]] <tab/>o <tab/><i>E. Q. corpus non est lapis. <tab/>E. Q. corpus non est lapis.</i><tab/>o\n [[1062.31]] <tab/>V.\n [[1062.32]] <tab/>Fris<tab/><i>Q. arbor est aegra</i>, <tab/><i>N. arbor est animal</i>, <tab/>Fe\n [[1062.33]] <tab/>esm <tab/><i>N. animal est arbor, <tab/>Q. aegrum est arbor</i>, <tab/>ri\n [[1062.34]] <tab/>o <tab/><i>E. Q. aegrum non est animal. <tab/>E. Q. aegrum non est animal.</i><tab/>o </petit> </p>\n<p> [[1062.35]] <k>Logicae Liber Quartus</k>, <i>Sive</i> <k>Logicae Specialis liber i.</k> <i>De Logica Apodictica.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1062.36]] <k>Cap. I</k>, De natura Apodicticae. </p>\n<p> [[1063.1]] 17. Ceterum versatur Apodictica Logica non circa quasvis res cognitioni nostrae\n[[1063.2]] obvias promiscue, uti Generalis Logica; sed circa <i>Necessarias</i> praecipue; aliquo tamen\n[[1063.3]] modo etiam <i>Contingentibus</i> rebus applicatur. </p>\n<p> [[1063.4]] 18. Sunt autem <i>res Necessariae</i> quae semper eodem modo se habent, nec arbitrio\n[[1063.5]] voluntarii agentis variantur; uti sunt <i>res Naturales</i>, earumque mutationes aliave attributa;\n[[1063.6]] item <i>res Mathematicae</i>, quae a materia abstractae dicuntur, <greek>tà kat' ăfaíresin ^%)/onta</greek>, ut\n[[1063.7]] cum Geometra <i>Triangulum</i>, <i>cubum</i>, <i>sphaeram</i> considerat, separans eas figuras cogitatione\n[[1063.8]] <b>a <i>ligno</b>, <i><b>lapide</b></i>, <i><b>cera</b></i>, <i><b>orichalco</b></i> <b>aliave quavis materia.</b> </p>\n<p> [[1063.9]] <k>Cap. XVII.</k> De Ordine didascalico. </p>\n<p> [[1063.10]] 14. Est quando ne suppetit quidem, quod de universalioribus demonstretur. Ex. g.\n[[1063.11]] <i>De triangulo, prout a rectilineo, plano curvilineo, sphaerico, cylindrico, conico etc.\n[[1063.12]] abstrahitur, nihil habet, quod demonstret Geometra</i>: <Fn>imo</Fn> <i>nihil quod de <b>speculo in\n[[1063.13]] genere</i>, <Fn>imo aequ[a]litas angulorum ob pla[num] tangens</Fn> <i>Catoptricus: ideo ille a triangulo rectilineo, hic a speculo plano orditur.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1063.14]] <k>Logicae Liber Quintus</k>, <i>qui est</i> <k>Specialis Logicae Liber II</k>, De Dialectica. </p>\n<p> [[1063.15]] <k>Cap. V</k>, De differentiis Maximarum, et usu. </p>\n<p> [[1063.16]] 17. Fuerunt hactenus directarum exempla Maximarum: sequitur, quomodo <k>Reflexivae</k>\n[[1063.17]] in usum adhibendae. </p>\n<p> [[1063.18]] 18. Si quis ita colligat: </p>\n<p> [[1063.19]] <i>Omne animal sensu praeditum est</i>, </p>\n<p> [[1063.20]] <i>E. Omnis piscis sensu praeditus est</i>,\n [[1063.21]] Maxima, quae argumentum dirigit, haec est, </p>\n<p> [[1063.22]] <i>Quod universaliter convenit generi, etiam speciei universaliter convenit</i>:\n [[1063.23]] Attamen ad constitutionem argumenti nihil confert; sufficit enim hanc minorem adjicere,\n[[1063.24]] <i>Omnis piscis est animal.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1063.25]] 19. Quod si Maxima ut <i>constituente</i> uti placet, ita tela argumenti texenda est: </p>\n<p> [[1063.26]] <i>Quod universaliter convenit generi, etiam speciei universaliter convenit</i>; </p>\n<p> [[1063.27]] <i>At sensu praeditum universaliter convenit generi, videlicet animali</i>; </p>\n<p> [[1063.28]] <i>Ergo sensu praeditum speciei quoque, nimirum pisci, universaliter convenit</i>, </p>\n<p> [[1063.29]] <i>Ergo Omnis piscis sensu est praeditus</i>. </p>\n<p> [[1064.1]] 20. Crypsi tamen adhuc involutum est argumentum, Syllogismus enim apparens, qui\n[[1064.2]] e tribus prioribus propositionibus conflatur, non est legitimus, cum pluribus quam tribus\n[[1064.3]] constet terminis. </p>\n<p> [[1064.4]] 21. Reducitur autem ad formam expressam hac dianoearum serie: </p>\n<p> [[1064.5]] <i>1. Quod universaliter convenit generi, etiam speciei universaliter convenit</i>; </p>\n<p> [[1064.6]] <i>2. E. Quod universaliter convenit animali, etiam cuilibet speciei animalis universaliter\n[[1064.7]] convenit</i>; </p>\n<p> [[1064.8]] <i>3, At sensu praeditum universaliter convenit animali</i>; </p>\n<p> [[1064.9]] <i>4. E. Sensu praeditum universaliter convenit cuilibet speciei animalis</i>; </p>\n<p> [[1064.10]] <i>5. E. Quaelibet animalis species universaliter participat</i> <greek>tò</greek> <i>sensu praeditum</i>; sive,\n[[1064.11]] <i>particeps est sensus</i> </p>\n<p> [[1064.12]] <i>6. Atqui piscis est animalis species</i>, </p>\n<p> [[1064.13]] <i>7. E. Piscis universaliter participat</i> <greek>tò</greek> <i>sensu praeditum</i>; </p>\n<p> [[1064.14]] <i>8. E. Omnis piscis sensu praeditus est</i>.\n [[1064.15]] A prima ad secundam <i>est contractio</i> sive <i>contractiva consequentia</i>; a secunda ad quartam\n[[1064.16]] <i>syllogismus</i>: a quarta ad quintam inversio relationis; a quinta et sexta ad septimam\n[[1064.17]] syllogismus; a septima ad octavam <i><b>aequipollentia reflexivae et directae</b></i>\n[[1064.18]] Enuntiationis. </p>\n",
  "number": "225.",
  "title": "Marginalien zu Jungius' Logica Hamburgensis",
  "date": "[Herbst 1678 bis Winter 1679/80 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:225. Marginalien zu Jungius' Logica Hamburgensis [Herbst 1678 bis Winter 1679/80 (?)] [Herbst 1678 bis Winter 1679/80 (?)] logicae generalis Liber Primus. De Notionibus. Cap. V. De Praedicamento Quantitatis. 17. Curva non plana est, quae in plano sita esse nequit, Am Rande: ^&.!! uti sunt, Helix cyl...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>